# Function / Export Comments

When creating or substantially editing code, add a short comment block above each function and each export that explains, at a very high level, what it does and why it exists.

## Requirements

- Place 1–3 short comment lines immediately above the function or export
- Cover **what** (purpose) and **why** (reason / role in the flow)
- Keep comments high-level — do not narrate implementation details line by line
- Prefer plain language over jargon when both are accurate
- Apply to exported and non-exported functions, including Vue `script setup` helpers and composable/script utilities

## Examples

```typescript
// Builds the keymap payload the keyboard expects so the UI can
// write layer assignments without re-encoding keycodes elsewhere.
export function buildKeymapPayload(layer: number, keys: number[]) {
  // ...
}
```

```typescript
// Resolves a display label for a keycode so the keymap grid can
// show human-readable names instead of raw IDs.
function resolveKeyLabel(keycode: number): string {
  // ...
}
```

## Avoid

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — restates the code / too low-level
// Loop through keys and push into array
function collectKeys(keys: number[]) {
  // ...
}

// ❌ BAD — missing why
// Handles keycodes
export function handleKeycode(code: number) {
  // ...
}
```
